tal, and I'm also adding a simple report formatter that outputs the total as a string. Now I want to double-check the ledger test to make sure this logic matches expectations.\n\nTracing through the test case: credit 9 brings total to 9, debit 4 brings it to 5, and the duplicate credit event is correctly ignored, keeping total at 5. Then applying an unknown kind returns an error while leaving the total unchanged, which confirms the behavior is correct. I'm ready to write the fixes now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1389,"cache_read_input_tokens":15143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1389,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"294ea610-ad48-4580-9ffc-ad27915c34c0","uuid":"e30014ee-25c8-4e10-ba6c-813ba6714b97"}
